    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Twin pregnancy, dichorionic diamniotic (O30.041)</content>. Normal anatomy in both twins; low-risk cell-free DNA; placenta clear of the cervix; cervical length 41 mm, which is reassuring. Blood pressure 104/62 mmHg. [S]<list><item>Continue aspirin.</item><item>Growth scan, blood count, and glucose challenge at 25 weeks.</item><item>Cervical length is not repeated routinely; any later measurement only for symptoms.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Iron deficiency anemia in pregnancy (O99.011)</content>. Hemoglobin 11.1 g/dL and ferritin 24 ng/mL: responding to oral iron, so intravenous iron is not needed. [S]<list><item>Continue ferrous sulfate every other day.</item><item>Recheck at 25 weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Nausea and vomiting of pregnancy (O21.9)</content>. Resolved. [S]<list><item>Doxylamine with pyridoxine stopped.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure and urine protein</td><td>Every prenatal visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>104/62 mmHg; urine protein negative</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fetal hearts and fundal height</td><td>Every prenatal visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Fetal hearts 150 and 146 per minute; fundal height 22 cm</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight gain (about 17 to 25 kg for twins from a normal BMI)</td><td>Every prenatal visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>61.5 kg, up 3.5 kg since intake</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Detailed anatomy scans with placental location</td><td>At 18 to 22 weeks</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Normal anatomy in both twins; placenta anterior and clear of the cervix</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Cervical length</td><td>At the anatomy scan; routine serial screening is not supported in twins</td><td>Completed today</td><td>41 mm by transvaginal scan</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Cell-free DNA screening</td><td>From 10 weeks, as she chose</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Low risk for trisomies 21, 18, and 13</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Hemoglobin and ferritin</td><td>At intake, at the anatomy-scan visit, at 24 to 28 weeks, and in the third trimester</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Hemoglobin 11.1 g/dL and ferritin 24 ng/mL; responding to oral iron</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Low-dose aspirin</td><td>Daily from 12 weeks until delivery; review at every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taken nightly since 12 weeks; no bruising or bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Growth scan with discordance</td><td>Every four weeks from about 20 to 24 weeks in a dichorionic twin pregnancy</td><td>Due</td><td>First growth scan booked at 25 weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Gestational diabetes screen</td><td>At 24 to 28 weeks</td><td>Due</td><td>At 25 weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Perinatal mood screen (EPDS)</td><td>Each trimester</td><td>Due</td><td>Second-trimester screen at 25 weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Preterm labor warning signs</td><td>Every prenatal visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Warning signs reviewed</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>The cause of the large uterus and the dating of the pregnancy established at the 11-week scan. Outcome by 2026-03-17: Dichorionic diamniotic twins; dating by her last period confirmed by the crown-rump lengths [S]</item><item>An informed choice about aneuploidy screening by 14 weeks. Outcome by 2026-03-17: Chose nuchal translucency for each twin with cell-free DNA; declined diagnostic testing for now [S]</item><item>Hemoglobin and ferritin in the normal range for pregnancy by the third trimester. In progress; target 2026-08-18 [S]</item><item>Growth discordance under 20 percent at every growth scan. In progress; target 2026-08-18 [S]</item><item>A written delivery plan agreed by 34 weeks. In progress; target 2026-08-18 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Multifetal Gestations: Twin, Triplet, and Higher-Order Multifetal Pregnancies: ACOG Practice Bulletin, Number 231 (2021); Prediction and Prevention of Spontaneous Preterm Birth: ACOG Practice Bulletin, Number 234 (2021); Screening for Fetal Chromosomal Abnormalities: ACOG Practice Bulletin, Number 226 (2020); Anemia in Pregnancy: ACOG Practice Bulletin, Number 233 (2021); Aspirin Use to Prevent Preeclampsia and Related Morbidity and Mortality: Preventive Medication (2021)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Prenatal visit with the growth scan, blood count, and glucose challenge at 25 weeks. Next scheduled visit 2026-06-23: prenatal visit at 25 weeks: growth scan, glucose challenge, and blood count. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
